        {
            "category": "gateway",
            "id": "R-01",
            "kind": "risk",
            "severity": "high",
            "text": "The gateway MAC changes at cutover: hosts cache 10.230.0.1 as 00:00:0c:9f:fb:b8; the fabric answers with 00:1c:73:00:00:99. A host updates its entry when the fabric gateway ARPs for it (the post-cutover ping of every baseline endpoint does this) or when the entry ages out; until then it sends to the old MAC. Ping every endpoint from the fabric gateway right after the cutover, and check hosts that do not answer."
        },
        {
            "category": "endpoints",
            "id": "R-02",
            "kind": "risk",
            "severity": "low",
            "text": "Re-run discovery or check them by hand: 1 active IP(s) are in ARP but not in any MAC table (aged out, or behind a switch that was not discovered)."
        },
